    {
      "page_title": "Scaling, Resilience and Design",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q47. How do you scale an API to handle 10x traffic?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Find the bottleneck first, then {green:scale out} stateless servers behind a load balancer and offload reads.",
            "Keep servers **stateless**: sessions live in Redis",
            "Cache hot reads; add DB read replicas",
            "Queue slow work; autoscale on CPU or latency"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "Client -> LB -> API x N",
            "API -> Redis cache -> DB replicas",
            "API -> Queue -> Workers"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q48. How do you make an API resilient with timeouts, retries and circuit breakers?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Bound every call with a ==timeout==, retry only safe failures, and trip a breaker when a dependency keeps failing.",
            "Retry with **exponential backoff** plus jitter",
            "Retry only idempotent calls or keyed requests",
            "Open breaker fails fast, then probes half-open"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "wait = min(cap, base * 2**n)",
            "wait = random(0, wait)   # jitter",
            "if breaker.open: return fallback()",
            "call(timeout=2)          # seconds"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "Closed",
                "sub": "calls pass",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "Open",
                "sub": "fail fast",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "Half-open",
                "sub": "probe calls",
                "ink": "orange"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q49. How would you design a URL shortener API?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Expose a create endpoint and a redirect endpoint, backed by a unique short code mapped to the long URL.",
            "`POST /urls` returns a code; `GET /{code}` sends **301/302**",
            "Generate codes via base62 counter ID",
            "Cache hot codes in Redis; DB stores the mapping"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /urls {\"url\":\"https://a.com/x\"}",
            "-> 201 {\"code\":\"aZ3k9\"}",
            "GET /aZ3k9 -> 302 Location: https://a.com/x"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Choice",
            "Trade-off"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Hash of URL",
              "Collisions, no counter"
            ],
            [
              "Counter + base62",
              "Unique, predictable"
            ],
            [
              "301 redirect",
              "Cached, loses click stats"
            ],
            [
              "302 redirect",
              "Every hit counted"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Q50. How would you design a payment API that never double-charges?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Require an ==idempotency key== per payment and make the charge a single atomic, stateful operation.",
            "Store key + result; replay it on any retry",
            "Use a **state machine**: created, authorized, captured, failed",
            "Reconcile with provider webhooks, never trust timeouts"
          ],
          "example_code": [
            "POST /payments",
            "Idempotency-Key: ord_81_try1",
            "-> 201 {\"id\":\"pay_9\",\"status\":\"captured\"}",
            "(retry) -> 200 same pay_9"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Design answer order",
          "text": "Clarify requirements, sketch the endpoints, then cover scale, failures and trade-offs."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "server",
      "aside": "design out loud!",
      "subtitle": "Resilience, URLs, payments"
    },
